bsd-tests.list
bsd.test
cov.out

# ⛔ A BACKGROUND CI WATCH LASTS SEVERAL TURNS BY CONSTRUCTION, so its output
# cannot live in a one-turn scratchpad — the scratchpad is wiped on reboot and
# the answer vanishes with it, which reads as "the watch reported nothing".
# It therefore goes in the clone, which is durable; and the clone is a
# repository, so it has to be ignored or it joins the next commit.
# go-zpkg/packages carries the same line for the same reason.
/.prwait-*.log

# The binaries `go build ./cmd/...` drops in the repository root. ⛔ None of
# these was ignored, and `bk` — this command's old name — sat in HEAD for three
# months at 19 771 746 bytes (10 575 333 on disk, of a ~15 MiB .git), referenced
# by nothing. Anchored with a leading slash so only the root build output is
# ignored, never a directory or a source file that happens to share the name.
/bk
/zbk
/zpkb
/venvlaunch
